{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20421",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.14,
      "end_seconds": 3.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "good morning, grab a seat"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.36,
      "end_seconds": 10.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, hello, thanks for fitting me in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.08,
      "end_seconds": 15.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "what's the the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.72,
      "end_seconds": 28.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "It's pain in my right ear. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.88,
      "end_seconds": 30.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Okay, since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.85,
      "end_seconds": 34.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "It It started yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.25,
      "end_seconds": 45.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.04,
      "end_seconds": 62.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.65,
      "text": "I get some relief from a warm cloth it feels moderate to me i notice it more with chewing and touching the ear it happens all the time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.28,
      "end_seconds": 65.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.65,
      "end_seconds": 78.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.41,
      "text": "Muffled hearing goes along with it, most of the the time. As for Muffled hearing, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.47,
      "end_seconds": 90.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any facial weakness, dizziness or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.3,
      "end_seconds": 93.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.53,
      "end_seconds": 99.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "has there been any swelling behind the ear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.9,
      "end_seconds": 103.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "No, no swelling behind the ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.6,
      "end_seconds": 107.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.0,
      "end_seconds": 111.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.09,
      "end_seconds": 117.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.75,
      "end_seconds": 122.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.51,
      "end_seconds": 136.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.97,
      "end_seconds": 143.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Sitagliptin. I take it 100 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.69,
      "end_seconds": 147.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.04,
      "end_seconds": 153.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.91,
      "end_seconds": 158.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.46,
      "end_seconds": 162.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.99,
      "end_seconds": 166.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "okay, any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.32,
      "end_seconds": 177.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "I had part of my thyroid removed years back i did try to ignore it for a while"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.77,
      "end_seconds": 181.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.86,
      "end_seconds": 198.51,
      "duration_seconds": 15.65,
      "text": "Mm, I have diabetes, for nearly five years. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.77,
      "end_seconds": 202.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.48,
      "end_seconds": 226.05,
      "duration_seconds": 21.57,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I've never touched a cigarette. My husband and I live above the shop. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.49,
      "end_seconds": 230.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.43,
      "end_seconds": 239.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.48,
      "end_seconds": 261.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, heart rate 80, pressure 114 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.34,
      "end_seconds": 263.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.32,
      "end_seconds": 270.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.62,
      "end_seconds": 303.28,
      "duration_seconds": 25.66,
      "text": "So, based on your history, it's hard to say. An outer ear canal infection is one possibility and a middle ear infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet. I'll start you on antibiotic and steroid ear drops, 3 drops, twice a day, for seven days. It's for ear canal infection. Keep the ear dry, no swimming, and don't poke anything into it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.03,
      "end_seconds": 312.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.82,
      "text": "cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.29,
      "end_seconds": 341.65,
      "duration_seconds": 28.36,
      "text": "Ah. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Keep an eye out, and if the ear swells or you get dizzy or feverish, call us the same day or go to emergency. Please come and see me if it isn't better in three days. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.61,
      "end_seconds": 347.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    }
  ]
}